        "id": 9274,
        "name": "SuperRick",
        "username": "SuperRick",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/superrick/{size}/2705_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-16T17:20:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I remember playing a MMO similar to SotM in that it had archtypes (and I know there's been many others), or different classifications of heroes.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here they were in that game:</p><p><strong>TANKS:</strong>&nbsp; Damage absorbers.&nbsp; They could redirect damage to themselves, and while they could punch a little,&nbsp;there was&nbsp;virturally no area-of-effect damage.&nbsp; Superman without nearly as much offensive potential.</p><p><strong>BLASTERS:</strong>&nbsp; Ranged damage dealers, heavy damage and heavy on the area-of-effect damage.&nbsp; They had glass jaws though,&nbsp;and would&nbsp;go down fast without some protection.&nbsp; Human torch.</p><p><strong>CONTROLLERS:</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Crowd control.&nbsp; They couldn't do much damage and they they weren't tough, but they could keep huge crouds wandering around in a daze or slipping on ice or something.&nbsp;&nbsp;They could buff and debuff a little.&nbsp; I'm thinking maybe Dr. Strange, I'm&nbsp;having a hard time thinking of one.</p><p><strong>DEFENDERS:&nbsp; </strong>Great for dealing out buffs and debuffs, as a secondary they could blast a little.&nbsp;&nbsp;Good healers.<strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>SCRAPPERS:</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Tough melee damage dealers with very little AOE.&nbsp; Not as tough as tanks, not as much damage as blasters.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Anyways, would these five archtypes fit SotM?&nbsp; If so, where would&nbsp;you put the heroes?&nbsp; It seems to me that Legacy is a tank; Ra, Fanatic, and Chrono-Ranger&nbsp;would be blasters; Visionary is a controller; Haka is a scrapper.&nbsp;&nbsp;Am I wrong on these?&nbsp; Where&nbsp;would you put the&nbsp;others?</p><p>I know, probably a noob question, but I'm just trying to&nbsp;better understand the game.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
