        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/superrick/{size}/2705_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-16T19:02:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So many heros fall into many of those catagories to varrying degrees.Legacy. He is every bit of your \"Tank\" as he is your \"Defender\" with strong chunks of \"Controller\"I do not see any hero as being so clear cut purely from a mechanical/gameplay perspective.Thematically however I think there is nothing wrong with how you see it. Very reminicent of City of Heros/DC Online catagories for hero creation.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, CoH is where I got those from.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I'm having difficulty putting the characters into the different categories as well.&nbsp; It's obvious they don't fit 100%, but if anyone wanted to  categorize  them \"where they leaned,\" that would be great for helping me better grasp the game (and explain it to others).</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Maybe just three categories:</strong></p>\n<p>Strong Tank (excells at absorbing damage)</p>\n<p>Strong Damage Dealer (excells at dealing damage)</p>\n<p>Strong Support (excells at crowd control, buffs and debuffs)</p>",
